Feature: Agent Log Calculated Field Query Specification

  The Agent Log calculated field query retrieves agent session and profile data, applies business logic for field derivation, and displays the calculated field(s) in the purgo_playground.agent_log table. The query must join session_tracking_data, user_presence_tracker, and agent_profile_data, handle hardcoded fields, generate a unique surrogate key, and apply all specified validation and error handling rules.

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the Schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the following source tables are available:
      | session_tracking_data      |
      | user_presence_tracker      |
      | agent_profile_data         |
    And the target table is "agent_log"
    And the following hardcoded values are required:
      | agent_city   | New York |
      | agent_state  | NY       |
      | agent_country| USA      |
      | agent_zip_code| 10001   |
    And the calculated field "agent_key" is generated by concatenating all agent_log fields and hashing the result using SHA256
    And the query is for display purposes only, not for insert/update

  Scenario Outline: Display calculated field for agent log with valid data
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with
      | person_identifier | <person_identifier> |
      | session_start_time| <session_start_time>|
      | session_end_time  | <session_end_time>  |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record with
      | person_identifier | <person_identifier> |
      | email_address     | <email_address>     |
    And agent_profile_data contains a record with
      | email_address         | <email_address>         |
      | internal_user_key     | <internal_user_key>     |
      | full_name             | <full_name>             |
      | last_modified_timestamp| <last_modified_timestamp>|
    When the query is executed for log_date = date(<session_start_time>)
    Then the output must include
      | unix_id              | <internal_user_key>      |
      | agent_name           | <full_name>              |
      | log_date             | date(<session_start_time>)|
      | agent_first_login    | min(session_start_time) for agent on log_date |
      | agent_first_logout   | max(session_end_time) for agent on log_date   |
      | total_login_time_hrs | (agent_first_logout - agent_first_login) in hours, formatted as string with 2 decimal places |
      | agent_city           | "New York"               |
      | agent_state          | "NY"                     |
      | agent_country        | "USA"                    |
      | agent_zip_code       | "10001"                  |
      | data_loaded_at       | current timestamp        |
      | agent_key            | SHA256(concat(all above fields)) |
    And all fields must be non-null except where source data is missing

    Examples:
      | person_identifier | session_start_time      | session_end_time        | email_address         | internal_user_key | full_name      | last_modified_timestamp |
      | AGT001            | 2025-01-02T08:00:00Z    | 2025-01-02T17:00:00Z    | agent1@company.com    | IU001            | John Doe       | 2025-01-01T12:00:00Z    |
      | AGT002            | 2025-01-03T09:15:00Z    | 2025-01-03T18:05:00Z    | agent2@company.com    | IU002            | Jane Smith     | 2025-01-02T09:00:00Z    |

  Scenario: Multiple sessions per agent per day
    Given session_tracking_data contains multiple records for person_identifier "AGT003" on "2025-01-04"
      | session_start_time      | session_end_time        |
      | 2025-01-04T07:55:00Z   | 2025-01-04T12:00:00Z    |
      | 2025-01-04T13:00:00Z   | 2025-01-04T17:30:00Z    |
    And user_presence_tracker contains a record for "AGT003" with email_address "agent3@company.com"
    And agent_profile_data contains a record for "agent3@company.com" with internal_user_key "IU003" and full_name "Alice Lee"
    When the query is executed for log_date = "2025-01-04"
    Then agent_first_login is "2025-01-04T07:55:00Z"
    And agent_first_logout is "2025-01-04T17:30:00Z"
    And total_login_time_hrs is "9.58"
    And agent_key is SHA256(concat(all output fields))

  Scenario: Multiple agent_profile_data records for same email_address
    Given agent_profile_data contains two records for email_address "agent4@company.com"
      | internal_user_key | full_name   | last_modified_timestamp   |
      | IU004             | Bob Brown   | 2025-01-01T10:00:00Z     |
      | IU004             | Robert Brown| 2025-01-02T11:00:00Z     |
    When the query is executed for person_identifier "AGT004"
    Then the output uses full_name "Robert Brown" (most recent last_modified_timestamp)

  Scenario: Missing person_identifier in session_tracking_data
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier NULL
    When the query is executed
    Then the output must not include a row for this record
    And an error is logged in agent_log_error_log with
      | error_type    | "Missing person_identifier" |
      | error_message | "person_identifier is NULL in session_tracking_data" |
      | error_time    | current timestamp           |

  Scenario: Missing email_address in user_presence_tracker
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record with person_identifier "AGT005"
    And user_presence_tracker does not contain a record for "AGT005"
    When the query is executed
    Then the output must not include a row for this record
    And an error is logged in agent_log_error_log with
      | error_type    | "Missing email_address" |
      | error_message | "No email_address found for person_identifier AGT005" |
      | error_time    | current timestamp       |

  Scenario: Missing agent_profile_data for email_address
    Given user_presence_tracker contains a record for person_identifier "AGT006" with email_address "agent6@company.com"
    And agent_profile_data does not contain a record for "agent6@company.com"
    When the query is executed
    Then the output must not include a row for this record
    And an error is logged in agent_log_error_log with
      | error_type    | "Missing agent_profile_data" |
      | error_message | "No agent_profile_data found for email_address agent6@company.com" |
      | error_time    | current timestamp            |

  Scenario: NULL session_start_time or session_end_time
    Given session_tracking_data contains a record for person_identifier "AGT007" with session_start_time NULL and session_end_time "2025-01-05T17:00:00Z"
    When the query is executed
    Then the output must not include a row for this record
    And an error is logged in agent_log_error_log with
      | error_type    | "Missing session times" |
      | error_message | "session_start_time or session_end_time is NULL for person_identifier AGT007" |
      | error_time    | current timestamp       |

  Scenario: Unique key generation validation
    Given all agent_log fields are populated for person_identifier "AGT008"
    When the query is executed
    Then agent_key is generated as SHA256(concat(unix_id, agent_name, log_date, agent_first_login, agent_first_logout, total_login_time_hrs, agent_city, agent_state, agent_country, agent_zip_code, data_loaded_at))
    And agent_key is a 64-character hexadecimal string

  Scenario Outline: Data type and format validation
    Given the query output includes the following fields
      | unix_id              | <unix_id>              |
      | agent_name           | <agent_name>           |
      | log_date             | <log_date>             |
      | agent_first_login    | <agent_first_login>    |
      | agent_first_logout   | <agent_first_logout>   |
      | total_login_time_hrs | <total_login_time_hrs> |
      | agent_city           | <agent_city>           |
      | agent_state          | <agent_state>          |
      | agent_country        | <agent_country>        |
      | agent_zip_code       | <agent_zip_code>       |
      | data_loaded_at       | <data_loaded_at>       |
      | agent_key            | <agent_key>            |
    Then unix_id is string and not null
    And agent_name is string and not null
    And log_date is date in "YYYY-MM-DD" format
    And agent_first_login and agent_first_logout are timestamps in "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS" format
    And total_login_time_hrs is string, formatted as decimal with 2 places
    And agent_city, agent_state, agent_country, agent_zip_code are strings and not null
    And data_loaded_at is timestamp and not null
    And agent_key is string, 64-character hexadecimal, not null

    Examples:
      | unix_id | agent_name | log_date    | agent_first_login     | agent_first_logout    | total_login_time_hrs | agent_city | agent_state | agent_country | agent_zip_code | data_loaded_at         | agent_key                                                                |
      | IU009   | Sam Green  | 2025-01-06  | 2025-01-06 08:00:00   | 2025-01-06 17:00:00   | 9.00                 | New York   | NY         | USA          | 10001         | 2025-01-06 17:01:00    | 7e3a1c2b4d... (64 hex chars)                                              |

  Scenario: Filter by date range
    Given session_tracking_data contains records for log_date between "2025-01-01" and "2025-01-07"
    When the query is executed with filter log_date >= "2025-01-02" and log_date <= "2025-01-06"
    Then only records with log_date in the specified range are included in the output

  Scenario: Filter by agent selection
    Given session_tracking_data contains records for person_identifier in ("AGT010", "AGT011", "AGT012")
    When the query is executed with filter person_identifier = "AGT011"
    Then only records for "AGT011" are included in the output

  Scenario: Output schema validation
    When the query is executed
    Then the output schema must match purgo_playground.agent_log:
      | unix_id              | string   | nullable |
      | agent_name           | string   | nullable |
      | log_date             | date     | nullable |
      | agent_first_login    | timestamp| nullable |
      | agent_first_logout   | timestamp| nullable |
      | total_login_time_hrs | string   | nullable |
      | agent_lunch_login    | timestamp| nullable |
      | agent_lunch_logout   | timestamp| nullable |
      | agent_lunch_duration | string   | nullable |
      | agent_city           | string   | nullable |
      | agent_state          | string   | nullable |
      | agent_country        | string   | nullable |
      | agent_zip_code       | string   | nullable |
      | data_loaded_at       | timestamp| nullable |
      | agent_key            | string   | nullable |

  Scenario: Error logging for all error scenarios
    Given any error occurs during query execution (missing data, invalid format, etc.)
    Then an error is logged in agent_log_error_log with
      | error_type    | <error_type>    |
      | error_message | <error_message> |
      | error_time    | current timestamp |

    Examples:
      | error_type                | error_message                                               |
      | Missing person_identifier | person_identifier is NULL in session_tracking_data          |
      | Missing email_address     | No email_address found for person_identifier AGT005         |
      | Missing agent_profile_data| No agent_profile_data found for email_address agent6@company.com |
      | Missing session times     | session_start_time or session_end_time is NULL for person_identifier AGT007 |
      | Data type mismatch        | Field agent_first_login is not a valid timestamp            |
      | Hashing error             | agent_key could not be generated due to null fields         |
